Certainly building on the fly would be better. We're not well suited for that at the moment but it will be possible soon(-ish).

For now, the approach you're using is OK. You could use R but you wouldn't gain that much:

custompopup5 <- paste0("<div><h3><b>You selected: </b></h3>", custompopup1, "</br></br><img src='", img, " width = '100'/></div>")

could become

custompopup5 <- lapply(custompopup1, function(popup) {
as.character(div(
h3(tags$b("You selected:")),
popup,
tags$br(),
tags$br(),
tags$img(src=img, width=100)
))
})

